{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וחי אחיך עמך", :translit "ve-chai achicha imcha", :gloss "and your brother shall live with you"} {:he "אל תקח מאתו נשך ותרבית", :translit "al tikach mimenu neshekh ve-tarbit", :gloss "do not take from him interest or increase"} {:he "בנשך נתן חיה לא יחיה", :translit "be-neshekh natan chichah lo yichyeh", :gloss "he gave at interest, took increase — shall he live? he shall not live"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah of adjacent verses: Lev 25:35 ends with 'live,' Lev 25:36 begins with 'do not take interest'"}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel 18:13 describes a man who lends at interest and asks 'shall he live? He shall not live.' The verse Leviticus 25:35 'and your brother shall live with you' is immediately followed by Leviticus 25:36 'do not take from him interest or increase,' linking the prohibition of interest directly to the theme of preserving life.", :sources ["Ezekiel 18:13" "Leviticus 25:35-36"]}} {:quotes [{:he "נשך", :translit "neshekh", :gloss "interest"} {:he "זה נחש", :translit "zeh nachash", :gloss "this [is] serpent"} {:he "ונחש עפר לחמו", :translit "ve-nachash afar lachmo", :gloss "and dust the serpent's food"} {:he "רבית", :translit "ribbit", :gloss "interest"} {:he "תרי\"ב", :translit "terei-vav", :gloss "six hundred twelve"} {:he "תרי\"ב מצות", :translit "terei-vav mitzvot", :gloss "612 commandments"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "נשך", :b "נחש"} {:kind :gematria, :a "רבית", :b "תרי\"ב"} {:kind :gematria, :a "רבית", :b "תרי\"ב מצות"}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 65:25 states 'and dust shall be the serpent's food,' understood as a decree that the serpent will never be healed. The serpent of Eden was cursed in Genesis 3:14 to eat dust. The Talmud compares the usurer to a serpent, noting that just as a serpent's bite is not immediately felt but ultimately kills, so too interest accumulates and destroys — this analogy is developed at Bava Metzia 71a. The six hundred thirteen commandments were received by Israel at Sinai as described in Makkot 23b-24a.", :sources ["Isaiah 65:25" "Genesis 3:14" "Bava Metzia 71a" "Makkot 23b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah of adjacent verses: Lev 25:35 ends with 'live,' Lev 25:36 begins with 'do not take interest'", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "נשך", :a-value 370, :b "נחש", :b-value 358, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "רבית", :a-value 612, :b "תרי\"ב", :b-value 612, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "רבית", :a-value 612, :b "תרי\"ב מצות", :b-value 1148, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:25:49.577749134Z", :model "glm-5.2"}